The `validate` function is an async function that validates the form data and returns an object of validation errors. If there are no errors, it returns an empty object. If there are errors, it calls the `formatErrors` function to format the errors into an object that can be used to provide feedback to the user.

The `formatErrors` function takes in a `yup.ValidationError` object and formats the errors into an object that has keys and values. The keys represent the paths of the form data that have errors, and the values represent the error messages.

